sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  title Journey 10: Complete Candidate Data Sovereignty, JSON Backup & Atomic Erasure

  actor User as Candidate
  participant Web as DataPrivacyModal.tsx
  participant Exporter as userDataExport.ts
  participant LocalStore as Browser LocalStorage
  participant DOM as Browser Document Engine

  User->>Web: Clicks "Privacy & Data" in navigation footer
  Web->>Exporter: exportAllCurevoData() scans all localStorage keys
  Exporter->>LocalStore: Reads draft, jobs, applications, sessions, stories, linkedin, research
  LocalStore-->>Exporter: JSON data chunks
  Exporter-->>Web: Summary metadata (e.g. 1 draft, 4 jobs, 2 applications, 1 interview)
  Web-->>User: Displays data sovereignty dashboard showing local data inventory

  User->>Web: Clicks "Download Unified JSON Backup"
  Web->>Exporter: downloadAllCurevoDataJson()
  Exporter->>DOM: Creates application/json Blob and triggers download "curevo_complete_backup_YYYY-MM-DD.json"
  DOM-->>User: Saves file to local computer disk

  opt Restore from Backup
    User->>Web: Uploads prior backup JSON file
    Web->>DOM: FileReader.readAsText(file) parses backup schema
    Web->>Exporter: importAllCurevoData(jsonText)
    Exporter->>LocalStore: Writes restored keys back into localStorage
    Exporter-->>Web: Dispatches onDataChanged() event
    Web-->>User: Hydrates full application state instantly
  end

  User->>Web: Clicks "Delete All Data"
  Web-->>User: Prompts with confirmation warning: "This action cannot be undone."
  User->>Web: Confirms deletion
  Web->>Exporter: clearAllCurevoData()
  Exporter->>LocalStore: removeItem() on all 8 Curevo keys
  Exporter->>Web: Resets all in-memory React component states to pristine empty defaults
  Web-->>User: Displays "All local data purged" confirmation toast
